@@ -23,6 +23,26 @@
 ```bash
 pip install -e .
 ```
+
+Install the packages whose members ScopeLens will analyze into the same Python
+environment, then prepare their disk parse cache:
+
+```bash
+python -m pip install -r /path/to/requirements.txt
+python -m scopelens.prepare_cache --modules /path/to/modules.txt --cache-home /path/to/cache
+XDG_CACHE_HOME=/path/to/cache scopelens
+```
+
+`modules.txt` lists import names, one per line (for example `numpy`, `seaborn`,
+`nltk`, and `docx` for the `python-docx` distribution). Blank lines and `#` comments
+are allowed. Preparation uses the real member provider, reports each module's
+member count and elapsed time, and exits unsuccessfully if a query fails or
+returns no members. Use the same environment and cache directory when starting
+the server. Existing cache files are retained.
+
+This prepares Jedi/Parso's disk parse cache; it does not persist inferred member
+lists or remove all first-query work in a new server. Changed sources still use
+Parso's normal cache validity checks.
 
